Burma (Myanmar)
Even during अशोक’s time (272-232 B. C.) बुद्धिस्म् had spread to Burma. The first Hindu kingdom had been established in the Arakan province by A.

) and settled down there. They gradually conquered the whole of Siam and Laos.
The first important kingdom of the Thais was that of Sukhodaya. Indrāditya was the first king and Sajjanālaya was the capital. Some names of this period like गान्धार and मिथिला as also Videha indicate the continuing influence of हिन्दु चुल्तुरे. Other names like Suvarṇagrāma, Unmārga Śilā, Haripuñjaya as well as the use of पाली language in the inscriptions and, construction of temples of Gupta style of architecture confirm this.
The Sukhodaya kingdom was succee-ded by अयोध्या kingdom—also spelt as ‘Ayuthia’—in A.
